TURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T01:00:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lasswellt/lasswellt/commit/c606ed6de46280baf37eb1860cc0ad1b50e0ed10","node_id":"C_kwDONmL2l9oAKGM2MDZlZDZkZTQ2MjgwYmFmMzdlYjE4NjBjYzBhZDFiNTBlMGVkMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasswellt/lasswellt/commit/b2d605fc52323b37be05e150cf94690ccf484838","sha":"b2d605fc52323b37be05e150cf94690ccf484838","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasswellt/lasswellt/commits/b2d605fc52323b37be05e150cf94690ccf484838"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/lasswellt/lasswellt/commit/144430fed726a185599cad3a0db0d5fd7a5618e2","sha":"144430fed726a185599cad3a0db0d5fd7a5618e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasswellt/lasswellt/commits/144430fed726a185599cad3a0db0d5fd7a5618e2"}],"sha":"c606ed6de46280baf37eb1860cc0ad1b50e0ed10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasswellt/lasswellt/commits/c606ed6de46280baf37eb1860cc0ad1b50e0ed10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/556374?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lasswellt","id":556374,"login":"lasswellt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NjM3NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lasswellt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasswellt/lasswellt/commits/144430fed726a185599cad3a0db0d5fd7a5618e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:44:57Z","email":"lasswellt@gmail.com","name":"Tom Lasswell"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:44:57Z","email":"lasswellt@gmail.com","name":"Tom Lasswell"},"message":"Add Home Assistant and Omarchy sections\n\nSplits the Code section into three named areas instead of one highlight\nplus a catch-all table.\n\nHome Assistant:\n- Govee, with the HACS default registry acceptance (hacs/default #5135,\n  merged 2026-01-19) called out — it installs without adding a custom\n  repository, which nothing on the page said\n- Navien NaviLink promoted out of the catch-all table: gold quality\n  scale, and a hand-written asyncio NaviLink client (REST auth, SigV4\n  WebSocket signing, MQTT) with no boto3 or AWSIoTPythonSDK\n\nOmarchy:\n- Both bar plugins promoted out of the catch-all table, where they were\n  described only as \"status bar widgets\". Both are service + bar-widget\n  plugins (v0.2.0 / v0.3.0, MIT) that publish a usage record in\n  Omarchy''s first-party collector contract, so the built-in Agents\n  panel and the plugin''s own panel read one file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b09ff24fe9b1db9f8f961bd437c5a330b9ee292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasswellt/lasswellt/git/trees/6b09ff24fe9b1db9f8f961bd437c5a330b9ee292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lasswellt/lasswellt/git/commits/144430fed726a185599cad3a0db0d5fd7a5618e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b09ff24fe9b1db9f8f961bd437c5a330b9ee292\nparent b2d605fc52323b37be05e150cf94690ccf484838\nauthor Tom Lasswell <lasswellt@gmail.com> 1789951497 -0400\ncommitter Tom Lasswell <lasswellt@gmail.com> 1789951497 -0400\n\nAdd Home Assistant and Omarchy sections\n\nSplits the Code section into three named areas instead of one highlight\nplus a catch-all table.\n\nHome Assistant:\n- Govee, with the HACS default registry acceptance (hacs/default #5135,\n  merged 2026-01-19) called out — it installs without adding a custom\n  repository, which nothing on the page said\n- Navien NaviLink promoted out of the catch-all table: gold quality\n  scale, and a hand-written asyncio NaviLink client (REST auth, SigV4\n  WebSocket signing, MQTT) with no boto3 or AWSIoTPythonSDK\n\nOmarchy:\n- Both bar plugins promoted out of the catch-all table, where they were\n  described only as \"status bar widgets\". Both are service + bar-widget\n  plugins (v0.2.0 / v0.3.0, MIT) that publish a usage record in\n  Omarchy''s first-party collector contract, so the built-in Agents\n  panel and the plugin''s own panel read one file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxrdgnaELzZfan4pKqdtunnt03k\nDT/vz/AiishxzNSDQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHmLDu+J4njE1NChAUnSC9PV03Kb+hCosodFbJeglGvM6OXdGqcL+04rNdf76GLvOw\nlKIV+i2g5urocOQiADEwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T00:45:00Z"}}